{"jobs":[{"id":"c7ec4593-32be-462f-b834-d3ca45b20a2c","title":"Healthcare Coordinator","department":"Care Delivery","team":"Care Delivery","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote (US)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-15T16:38:23.037+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Austin"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/c7ec4593-32be-462f-b834-d3ca45b20a2c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/c7ec4593-32be-462f-b834-d3ca45b20a2c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Title:</strong> Healthcare Coordinator<br /><strong>Location:</strong> 100% Remote (US Only)<br /><strong>Compensation:</strong> $45,000-$55,000 + Full Benefits Package</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The <strong>Healthcare Coordinator</strong> plays a critical role in Telemedica's evolving care delivery model. This position supports the clinical readiness process for veterans seeking medical evidence for VA disability claims and lays the groundwork for expanded clinical services, including future offerings that may serve veteran family members and caregivers. Coordinators ensure timely and accurate completion of intake and documentation tasks, enabling high-quality care delivery across current and future service lines. As Telemedica advances its integrated care model, this role will be foundational in supporting multi-disciplinary coordination and clinical operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will do (Immediate):</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate care preparation activities, including intake form readiness and documentation tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with veterans to gather, verify, and clarify necessary information prior to service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support basic billing-related tasks, including confirming payment status, collecting payments, and flagging payment issues for resolution, until full customer service transition is complete</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect, organize, and upload medical records and supporting documents to clinical systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confirm appointment logistics and ensure veteran readiness ahead of scheduled services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor CRM/EHR task queues and ensure timely resolution of assigned workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point of contact for veterans navigating the intake-to-service process</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will do (Long-Term):</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the development of streamlined care coordination workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support initiatives to expand services beyond medical evidence into broader care delivery for veterans and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with QA, Provider Network Management, and clinical leadership to enhance service continuity and provider readiness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in data-informed process improvements and clinical readiness initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a resource for future clinical integration efforts, including RN-led and multidisciplinary team support</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will bring: </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Communicator:</strong> Able to convey complex information clearly and empathetically to patients, providers, and internal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible and Adaptable:</strong> Comfortable navigating evolving workflows, shifting priorities, and supporting transitional responsibilities during organizational change.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative:</strong> Works effectively across clinical, administrative, and operational teams to ensure seamless service delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Innovative Problem Solver:</strong> Takes initiative to streamline processes, improve veteran experience, and adapt to challenges with a solution-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Detail-Oriented:</strong> Maintains accuracy in scheduling, documentation, and intake processes to support timely, high-quality care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven:</strong> Demonstrates a deep commitment to serving veterans with respect, urgency, and compassion.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare coordination, medical office support, or similar clinical operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of medical documentation and patient communication</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and ability to manage multiple cases simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM, EHR, or care management platforms</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a telehealth or virtual care coordination setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in multidisciplinary medical practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the VA disability process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to care delivery models or integrated clinical teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation and Benefits:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Healthcare:</strong> PPO and HSA plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Retirement:</strong> 401(k) with up to 3% employer match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Spending:</strong> Health Savings Account (HSA) and Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Paid Time Off:</strong> 30 Days Paid Time Off (PTO), plus 14 paid holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Insurance:</strong> Short and Long-Term Disability, Life Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family &amp; Medical Leave:</strong> Paid Parental Leave, Military Leave, and Bereavement Leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Other Benefits:</strong> Employee discounts, Jury Duty Pay, Time-Off to Vote, and more</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><br />This position is <u>NOT APPLICABLE</u> to residents of: Alabama, California, Colorado, Kentucky, Montana, New York, North Dakota, Ohio, Oregon, Washington, Wyoming.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Telemedica</strong> is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, disability or any other basis prohibited by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Job Title: Healthcare Coordinator\nLocation: 100% Remote (US Only)\nCompensation: $45,000-$55,000 + Full Benefits Package\n\n\n\nThe Healthcare Coordinator plays a critical role in Telemedica's evolving care delivery model. This position supports the clinical readiness process for veterans seeking medical evidence for VA disability claims and lays the groundwork for expanded clinical services, including future offerings that may serve veteran family members and caregivers. Coordinators ensure timely and accurate completion of intake and documentation tasks, enabling high-quality care delivery across current and future service lines. As Telemedica advances its integrated care model, this role will be foundational in supporting multi-disciplinary coordination and clinical operations.\n\n\n\nWhat you will do (Immediate):\n\n - Coordinate care preparation activities, including intake form readiness and documentation tracking\n\n - Communicate with veterans to gather, verify, and clarify necessary information prior to service\n\n - Support basic billing-related tasks, including confirming payment status, collecting payments, and flagging payment issues for resolution, until full customer service transition is complete\n\n - Collect, organize, and upload medical records and supporting documents to clinical systems\n\n - Confirm appointment logistics and ensure veteran readiness ahead of scheduled services\n\n - Monitor CRM/EHR task queues and ensure timely resolution of assigned workflows\n\n - Serve as the primary point of contact for veterans navigating the intake-to-service process\n\n\n\nWhat you will do (Long-Term):\n\n - Contribute to the development of streamlined care coordination workflows\n\n - Support initiatives to expand services beyond medical evidence into broader care delivery for veterans and their families\n\n - Collaborate with QA, Provider Network Management, and clinical leadership to enhance service continuity and provider readiness\n\n - Participate in data-informed process improvements and clinical readiness initiatives\n\n - Serve as a resource for future clinical integration efforts, including RN-led and multidisciplinary team support\n\n\n\nWhat you will bring: \n\n - Strong Communicator: Able to convey complex information clearly and empathetically to patients, providers, and internal teams.\n\n - Flexible and Adaptable: Comfortable navigating evolving workflows, shifting priorities, and supporting transitional responsibilities during organizational change.\n\n - Collaborative: Works effectively across clinical, administrative, and operational teams to ensure seamless service delivery.\n\n - Innovative Problem Solver: Takes initiative to streamline processes, improve veteran experience, and adapt to challenges with a solution-oriented mindset.\n\n - Detail-Oriented: Maintains accuracy in scheduling, documentation, and intake processes to support timely, high-quality care.\n\n - Mission-Driven: Demonstrates a deep commitment to serving veterans with respect, urgency, and compassion.\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications:\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare coordination, medical office support, or similar clinical operations\n\n - Strong understanding of medical documentation and patient communication\n\n - High attention to detail and ability to manage multiple cases simultaneously\n\n - Experience with CRM, EHR, or care management platforms\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n - Experience in a telehealth or virtual care coordination setting\n\n - Experience in multidisciplinary medical practices\n\n - Familiarity with the VA disability process\n\n - Exposure to care delivery models or integrated clinical teams\n\n\n\nCompensation and Benefits:\n\n - Healthcare: PPO and HSA plans\n\n - Retirement: 401(k) with up to 3% employer match\n\n - Flexible Spending: Health Savings Account (HSA) and Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA)\n\n - Paid Time Off: 30 Days Paid Time Off (PTO), plus 14 paid holidays\n\n - Insurance: Short and Long-Term Disability, Life Insurance\n\n - Family & Medical Leave: Paid Parental Leave, Military Leave, and Bereavement Leave\n\n - Other Benefits: Employee discounts, Jury Duty Pay, Time-Off to Vote, and more\n\n\nThis position is NOT APPLICABLE to residents of: Alabama, California, Colorado, Kentucky, Montana, New York, North Dakota, Ohio, Oregon, Washington, Wyoming.\n\n\n\nTelemedica is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, disability or any other basis prohibited by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$45K – $55K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$45K - $55K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"67ae57f1-325c-49ba-b07a-c063d06f4f0e","tierSummary":"$45K – $55K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"546e02c8-4c63-49f2-889d-ec498bbf0d8b","summary":"$45K – $55K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":45000,"maxValue":55000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":45000,"maxValue":55000}]}},{"id":"339ba3f8-b75c-4558-93cb-473e07c85431","title":"Coach On Demand","department":"Care Delivery","team":"Care Delivery","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote (US)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-27T20:14:33.851+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Austin"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/339ba3f8-b75c-4558-93cb-473e07c85431","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/339ba3f8-b75c-4558-93cb-473e07c85431/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Position Summary</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <em>Served with Honor</em>, we believe every veteran and their family carries a story that deserves to be heard, honored, and supported. As a <strong>Coach On Demand</strong>, you will play a pivotal and compassionate role in bringing that belief to life by serving as a client-facing, on demand coach / consultant with strong sales expertise in positioning services / service plans to educate U.S. military veterans in navigating the confusing VA disability claims process. You will work with initial relationship holders, Care Support Partners, to be available in the moment to be a trusted advisor to U.S. military veterans by coaching, educating, and mentoring them through the confusing VA disability claim process, secure services /or service plans, and provide on-going coaching. In parallel, you will drive new sales through phone / text outreach to engage veterans who initiated interest and deliver coaching, education and mentoring as a subject matter to enroll in services / service plans and continue forward as the primary relationship holder. Our ideal candidates have strong sales skills, communications, and expertise in VA disability benefits; are highly motivated, self-starters with demonstrated experience in managing all aspects of the sales cycle from outreach to close / delivery with integrity, resourcefulness, and passion to make a difference for U.S. military veterans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Functions</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Serve as the primary relationship holder for new veterans and trusted point of contact either through Coach on Demand introduction and/or direct outreach (sales tactics)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Conduct thorough intake assessments to identify individual needs, goals, and barriers to achieving increased disability benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Reviews and understands each Veteran’s specific disability and analyzes to determine best strategy based on conditions and/or medical evidence the veteran client(s) may qualify for to maximize disability benefits</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Conducts VA disability claims coaching/consulting/strategy/sales services for veteran clients to include evaluation of medical evidence needs, speed to submission and maximization of benefits</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Educate veterans in access / use of client portal to select services / service plans, build engagement through tasks and chat, demonstrate the benefits to support a personalized experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Provides virtual support to the book of Veteran clients you source through daily email exchanges, phone calls, text messages, and video teleconference education-based coaching sessions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Detailed management and documentation of all sales and delivery activities within Salesforce CRM including pipeline reporting, conversion rates, etc.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Complies with all internal policies and all applicable state, local, and federal laws</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate and collaborate cross-functionally with internal business lines and service teams to ensure seamless delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Actively participate in team meetings, case reviews, and initiatives aimed at improving the client's experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build high-trust personal relationships with Veteran clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient in Sales CRM systems, preferably Salesforce with a strong skillset in services based sales, sales funnel management and dynamic selling of cross-functional services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to build rapport, maintain trust, and follow through on commitments to those served.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Strong Listening, Understanding, and empathy skills</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Strong organizational and time management skills</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal and written communication skills with the ability to engage compassionately and effectively in a virtual setting.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Must be a critical thinker with innovative problem-solving skills</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Strong presentation skills and experience with leading live Q&amp;A sessions</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, with the ability to convey complex information in a clear and understandable manner.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable navigating digital tools, CRM systems, omnichannel platforms, and resource databases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to learn new processes and adapt to changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Superior problem solving and organizational skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team-oriented, adaptable, and energized by a mission-driven, fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Bachelor’s degree required in Communications, Healthcare Administration, or related field from an accredited institution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· A minimum of 3-5 years of direct sales experience with services based sales ideally working in a the delivery of benefits to Veterans, and Veterans community</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in remote care coordination, digital navigation, and case management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse populations with empathy, humility, and respect for cultural differences.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sales experience in a start-up environment with focus on services based sales</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous knowledge and experience navigating the VA disability benefits system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with VA benefit systems, navigation and services, healthcare and/or behavioral health services with public/private community service programs is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of employment services, workforce development, or veteran transition programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting military families or individuals transitioning from active duty.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Physical Demands</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· This is a fully remote position. Candidates must have a secure, quiet workspace that ensures confidentiality and professionalism during client engagements.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must be able to sit and work at a computer for extended periods with access to a stable internet connection.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"Position Summary\n\nAt Served with Honor, we believe every veteran and their family carries a story that deserves to be heard, honored, and supported. As a Coach On Demand, you will play a pivotal and compassionate role in bringing that belief to life by serving as a client-facing, on demand coach / consultant with strong sales expertise in positioning services / service plans to educate U.S. military veterans in navigating the confusing VA disability claims process. You will work with initial relationship holders, Care Support Partners, to be available in the moment to be a trusted advisor to U.S. military veterans by coaching, educating, and mentoring them through the confusing VA disability claim process, secure services /or service plans, and provide on-going coaching. In parallel, you will drive new sales through phone / text outreach to engage veterans who initiated interest and deliver coaching, education and mentoring as a subject matter to enroll in services / service plans and continue forward as the primary relationship holder. Our ideal candidates have strong sales skills, communications, and expertise in VA disability benefits; are highly motivated, self-starters with demonstrated experience in managing all aspects of the sales cycle from outreach to close / delivery with integrity, resourcefulness, and passion to make a difference for U.S. military veterans.\n\n\n\n\n\nEssential Functions\n\n· Serve as the primary relationship holder for new veterans and trusted point of contact either through Coach on Demand introduction and/or direct outreach (sales tactics)\n\n· Conduct thorough intake assessments to identify individual needs, goals, and barriers to achieving increased disability benefits.\n\n· Reviews and understands each Veteran’s specific disability and analyzes to determine best strategy based on conditions and/or medical evidence the veteran client(s) may qualify for to maximize disability benefits\n\n· Conducts VA disability claims coaching/consulting/strategy/sales services for veteran clients to include evaluation of medical evidence needs, speed to submission and maximization of benefits\n\n· Educate veterans in access / use of client portal to select services / service plans, build engagement through tasks and chat, demonstrate the benefits to support a personalized experience.\n\n· Provides virtual support to the book of Veteran clients you source through daily email exchanges, phone calls, text messages, and video teleconference education-based coaching sessions\n\n· Detailed management and documentation of all sales and delivery activities within Salesforce CRM including pipeline reporting, conversion rates, etc.\n\n· Complies with all internal policies and all applicable state, local, and federal laws\n\n - Communicate and collaborate cross-functionally with internal business lines and service teams to ensure seamless delivery.\n\n - Actively participate in team meetings, case reviews, and initiatives aimed at improving the client's experience.\n\n\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n\n - Ability to build high-trust personal relationships with Veteran clients\n\n - Proficient in Sales CRM systems, preferably Salesforce with a strong skillset in services based sales, sales funnel management and dynamic selling of cross-functional services\n\n - Proven ability to build rapport, maintain trust, and follow through on commitments to those served.\n\n· Strong Listening, Understanding, and empathy skills\n\n· Strong organizational and time management skills\n\n - Strong interpersonal and written communication skills with the ability to engage compassionately and effectively in a virtual setting.\n\n· Must be a critical thinker with innovative problem-solving skills\n\n· Strong presentation skills and experience with leading live Q&A sessions\n\n - Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, with the ability to convey complex information in a clear and understandable manner.\n\n - Comfortable navigating digital tools, CRM systems, omnichannel platforms, and resource databases.\n\n - Ability to learn new processes and adapt to changes.\n\n - Superior problem solving and organizational skills.\n\n - Team-oriented, adaptable, and energized by a mission-driven, fast-paced environment.\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n· Bachelor’s degree required in Communications, Healthcare Administration, or related field from an accredited institution.\n\n· A minimum of 3-5 years of direct sales experience with services based sales ideally working in a the delivery of benefits to Veterans, and Veterans community\n\n - Experience in remote care coordination, digital navigation, and case management.\n\n - Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse populations with empathy, humility, and respect for cultural differences.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Strong sales experience in a start-up environment with focus on services based sales\n\n - Previous knowledge and experience navigating the VA disability benefits system\n\n - Experience with VA benefit systems, navigation and services, healthcare and/or behavioral health services with public/private community service programs is a plus.\n\n - Knowledge of employment services, workforce development, or veteran transition programs.\n\n - Experience supporting military families or individuals transitioning from active duty.\n\nPhysical Demands\n\n· This is a fully remote position. Candidates must have a secure, quiet workspace that ensures confidentiality and professionalism during client engagements.\n\n - Must be able to sit and work at a computer for extended periods with access to a stable internet connection.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$4,583 per month • $55,000 – $200,000 Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"f0d1e377-4ba1-472d-92a5-68345b86f57e","tierSummary":"On Target Earnings (Non Recoverable Draw) $4,583 per month • $55,000 – $200,000 Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b109967e-bd46-4bfe-8f5d-e2d938f6031f","summary":"On Target Earnings (Non Recoverable Draw) $4,583 per month","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 MONTH","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":4583,"maxValue":4583},{"id":"b127307b-140a-4d58-8994-6c5ac7e79622","summary":"$55,000 – $200,000 Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":200000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 MONTH","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":4583,"maxValue":4583},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":55000,"maxValue":200000}]}},{"id":"fea1bd9d-3776-4672-a6e7-5fbc18a76ae9","title":"Client Service Support Specialist","department":"Care Delivery","team":"Care Delivery","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote (US)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-06T14:21:16.785+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Austin"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/fea1bd9d-3776-4672-a6e7-5fbc18a76ae9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/fea1bd9d-3776-4672-a6e7-5fbc18a76ae9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Remote - US</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Position Summary: </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Client Service Support Specialist is responsible for delivering personalized, accurate, and compassionate assistance to clients, their family members, and their caregivers as they navigate complex issues related to support services. The Client Service Support Specialist’s goal is to ensure our clients feel heard, valued, and supported, and they will accomplish that goal by responding to inquiries with a balance of efficiency and empathy, ensuring  every interaction is meaningful and every concern is met with urgency and understanding.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Functions: </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">perform the essential functions. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Serve as the first point of contact for clients seeking support services, appeals, grievance, social service needs, billing issues, and insurance coverage. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Listen actively to client concerns, respond with empathy, and deliver accurate, timely solutions across communication channels (phone, chat, email). </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Support clients navigating complex issues including appeals and grievance submissions and status updates. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Billing discrepancies and insurance coverage clarifications. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Community-based SDOH-related referrals. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Escalations and compliance-sensitive concerns. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Provide warm handoffs to internal specialists or external partners when additional expertise or intervention is needed. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Document all interactions clearly and accurately in the CRM system to ensure continuity of care and compliance with policies. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Recognize urgent or high-risk issues and escalate appropriately using established protocols. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Maintain up-to-date knowledge of service offerings and regulations. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Collaborate cross-functionally with internal departments. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Participate in quality improvement efforts, team meetings, and feedback sessions to ensure excellent client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Bachelor’s degree required</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• A minimum of 3 years of customer experience in a healthcare contact center setting</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience in a virtual contact center with digital navigation preferred</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse populations with empathy, humility, and respect for cultural differences</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, able to simplify complex information with compassion and clarity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Familiarity with billing processes, insurance plans, appeals, and grievance resolution</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Understanding of Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) and ability to guide clients toward </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">appropriate resources</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Ability to remain calm and professional under pressure, especially when handling escalations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Demonstrated problem-solving skills and resourcefulness in navigating client needs</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Experience working with HIPAA-regulated data and maintaining client confidentiality</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Comfortable using CRM systems, ticketing platforms and digital communication tools</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Strong organizational skills with attention to detail and follow-through</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Ability to learn new processes and adapt to changes</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Team-oriented, adaptable, and energized by a mission-driven, fast-paced environment</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Use initiative to identify problems and provide solutions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Exceptional problem-solving and time management skills</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Served with Honor</strong> is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, disability or any other basis prohibited by law.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div>","descriptionPlain":"Location: Remote - US\n\n\n\nPosition Summary: \n\nThe Client Service Support Specialist is responsible for delivering personalized, accurate, and compassionate assistance to clients, their family members, and their caregivers as they navigate complex issues related to support services. The Client Service Support Specialist’s goal is to ensure our clients feel heard, valued, and supported, and they will accomplish that goal by responding to inquiries with a balance of efficiency and empathy, ensuring  every interaction is meaningful and every concern is met with urgency and understanding.\n\n\n\nEssential Functions: \n\nReasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to \n\nperform the essential functions. \n\n• Serve as the first point of contact for clients seeking support services, appeals, grievance, social service needs, billing issues, and insurance coverage. \n\n• Listen actively to client concerns, respond with empathy, and deliver accurate, timely solutions across communication channels (phone, chat, email). \n\n• Support clients navigating complex issues including appeals and grievance submissions and status updates. \n\n• Billing discrepancies and insurance coverage clarifications. \n\n• Community-based SDOH-related referrals. \n\n• Escalations and compliance-sensitive concerns. \n\n• Provide warm handoffs to internal specialists or external partners when additional expertise or intervention is needed. \n\n• Document all interactions clearly and accurately in the CRM system to ensure continuity of care and compliance with policies. \n\n• Recognize urgent or high-risk issues and escalate appropriately using established protocols. \n\n• Maintain up-to-date knowledge of service offerings and regulations. \n\n• Collaborate cross-functionally with internal departments. \n\n• Participate in quality improvement efforts, team meetings, and feedback sessions to ensure excellent client experience.\n\n\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n\n• Bachelor’s degree required\n\n• A minimum of 3 years of customer experience in a healthcare contact center setting\n\n• Experience in a virtual contact center with digital navigation preferred\n\n• Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse populations with empathy, humility, and respect for cultural differences\n\n• Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, able to simplify complex information with compassion and clarity\n\n• Familiarity with billing processes, insurance plans, appeals, and grievance resolution\n\n• Understanding of Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) and ability to guide clients toward \n\nappropriate resources\n\n• Ability to remain calm and professional under pressure, especially when handling escalations\n\n• Demonstrated problem-solving skills and resourcefulness in navigating client needs\n\n• Experience working with HIPAA-regulated data and maintaining client confidentiality\n\n• Comfortable using CRM systems, ticketing platforms and digital communication tools\n\n• Strong organizational skills with attention to detail and follow-through\n\n• Ability to learn new processes and adapt to changes\n\n• Team-oriented, adaptable, and energized by a mission-driven, fast-paced environment\n\n• Use initiative to identify problems and provide solutions\n\n• Exceptional problem-solving and time management skills\n\n\n\nServed with Honor is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, disability or any other basis prohibited by law.\n\n ","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$40K – $50K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$40K - $50K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f71dfb3a-ced9-4122-adce-1afebe9d352d","tierSummary":"Annual Base Salary Range $40K – $50K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"fda4f1a1-6590-444d-b5f0-716b08222fe8","summary":"Annual Base Salary Range $40K – $50K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":40000,"maxValue":50000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":40000,"maxValue":50000}]}},{"id":"08baa38c-0200-4095-b6b7-d6a190b06381","title":"Accounting Manager","department":"Accounting/Finance","team":"Accounting/Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote (US)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-05T13:55:08.016+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Austin"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/08baa38c-0200-4095-b6b7-d6a190b06381","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/08baa38c-0200-4095-b6b7-d6a190b06381/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Positions Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an experienced Accounting Manager to join our team in a fast-paced services environment. This is a key role responsible for ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial data, systems, and reporting while supporting strategic decision-making across the organization.<br /><br />As a trusted business partner to the Chief Financial Officer and Senior Leadership Team, the Accounting Manager will lead all aspects of accounting while contributing to financial planning and operational analysis. This role oversees the month-end close process including variance analysis while also operating as key resources in the annual budgeting, quarterly forecasting, and reporting to our leadership team.<br /><br />The ideal candidate will bring strong financial leadership, the ability to translate financial data into actionable insights and a deep understanding of NetSuite and financial systems. This position plays a critical role in strengthening financial controls, driving continuous improvement, and optimizing profitability while supporting effective cost management throughout the business.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Supervisory Responsibilities</strong>:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervises employees in the Accounting and Finance department. Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization's policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring, training employees, planning, assigning, and directing work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Functions and Responsibilities:</strong> Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Prepares accurate and timely monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Oversee general ledger maintenance, bank reconciliations, payroll, and end-of-month and year-end closing processes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Ensures financial records adhere to Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and regulatory standards.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Drive best practices in NetSuite ERP across all areas of the business; serve as a financial systems resource for Served with Honor.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Supervise, train, and mentor accounting staff.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Assists with budget preparation, cash management, and forecasting, while analyzing variances between budgeted and actual costs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Assists with preparation for audits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Coordinates with and prepares reports for CFO and upper management.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Contributes to team efforts by accomplishing related tasks as needed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Works across all levels of the organization to resolve issues, improve processes, and assist in the education and training of staff.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Performs other duties as assigned.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Bachelor’s degree in Accounting required; CPA strongly preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· 5+ years of progressive accounting and finance experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Strong GAAP and variance analysis expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Experience with NetSuite ERP systems required.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Demonstrated ability to lead and manage accounting staff and cross-functional teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Strong analytical, financial modeling, and communication skills; advanced Excel required; Power BI or similar reporting tools a plus.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Proven ability to work effectively with all levels of the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Experience implementing and optimizing Accounting and Finance technology platforms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Exceptional communication, coaching, and relationship-building skills</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Ability to think strategically while executing effectively in a fast-paced, evolving environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Demonstrated ability to build, develop, and lead high-performing teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Physical Demands:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Ability to stand, sit, use of hands to handle, feel, or reach with hands and arms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Ability to lift and/ or move up to 15 pounds.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and distance vision.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Environment:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">· Remote office environment</p>","descriptionPlain":"Positions Summary:\n\nWe are seeking an experienced Accounting Manager to join our team in a fast-paced services environment. This is a key role responsible for ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial data, systems, and reporting while supporting strategic decision-making across the organization.\n\nAs a trusted business partner to the Chief Financial Officer and Senior Leadership Team, the Accounting Manager will lead all aspects of accounting while contributing to financial planning and operational analysis. This role oversees the month-end close process including variance analysis while also operating as key resources in the annual budgeting, quarterly forecasting, and reporting to our leadership team.\n\nThe ideal candidate will bring strong financial leadership, the ability to translate financial data into actionable insights and a deep understanding of NetSuite and financial systems. This position plays a critical role in strengthening financial controls, driving continuous improvement, and optimizing profitability while supporting effective cost management throughout the business.\n\n\nSupervisory Responsibilities:\n\nSupervises employees in the Accounting and Finance department. Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization's policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring, training employees, planning, assigning, and directing work.\n\n\n\nEssential Functions and Responsibilities: Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\n· Prepares accurate and timely monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements.\n\n· Oversee general ledger maintenance, bank reconciliations, payroll, and end-of-month and year-end closing processes.\n\n· Ensures financial records adhere to Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and regulatory standards.\n\n· Drive best practices in NetSuite ERP across all areas of the business; serve as a financial systems resource for Served with Honor.\n\n· Supervise, train, and mentor accounting staff.\n\n· Assists with budget preparation, cash management, and forecasting, while analyzing variances between budgeted and actual costs.\n\n· Assists with preparation for audits.\n\n· Coordinates with and prepares reports for CFO and upper management.\n\n· Contributes to team efforts by accomplishing related tasks as needed.\n\n· Works across all levels of the organization to resolve issues, improve processes, and assist in the education and training of staff.\n\n· Performs other duties as assigned.\n\n\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n\n· Bachelor’s degree in Accounting required; CPA strongly preferred.\n\n· 5+ years of progressive accounting and finance experience.\n\n· Strong GAAP and variance analysis expertise.\n\n· Experience with NetSuite ERP systems required.\n\n· Demonstrated ability to lead and manage accounting staff and cross-functional teams.\n\n· Strong analytical, financial modeling, and communication skills; advanced Excel required; Power BI or similar reporting tools a plus.\n\n· Proven ability to work effectively with all levels of the organization.\n\n· Experience implementing and optimizing Accounting and Finance technology platforms.\n\n· Exceptional communication, coaching, and relationship-building skills\n\n· Ability to think strategically while executing effectively in a fast-paced, evolving environment.\n\n· Demonstrated ability to build, develop, and lead high-performing teams.\n\n\n\nPhysical Demands:\n\n· Ability to stand, sit, use of hands to handle, feel, or reach with hands and arms.\n\n· Ability to lift and/ or move up to 15 pounds.\n\n· Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and distance vision.\n\n\n\nWork Environment:\n\n· Remote office environment","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"50934112-226c-416c-a2a9-bb1ad997973e","title":"Finance Manager","department":"Accounting/Finance","team":"Accounting/Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote (US)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-08T14:52:06.469+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Austin"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/50934112-226c-416c-a2a9-bb1ad997973e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/50934112-226c-416c-a2a9-bb1ad997973e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Positions Summary:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking an experienced Finance Manager to join our team in a fast-paced services environment. This is a key role responsible for ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial plans and forecasts, systems, and reporting while supporting strategic decision-making across the organization. <br /> <br />As a trusted business partner to the Chief Financial Officer and Senior Leadership Team, the Finance Manager will lead all aspects of financial planning and analysis while contributing to accounting and operational analysis. This role oversees the budgeting and forecasts process including variance analysis while also operating as key resources in the monthly and annual close process.  <br /> <br />The ideal candidate will bring strong financial leadership, the ability to translate financial data into actionable insights and a deep understanding of NetSuite and financial systems. This position plays a critical role in strengthening financial controls, driving continuous improvement, and optimizing profitability while supporting effective cost management throughout the business. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Supervisory Responsibilities</strong>:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervises employees in the Accounting and Finance department. Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization's policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring, training employees, planning, assigning, and directing work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Functions and Responsibilities:</strong> Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and lead the revenue, expense and cash forecasting process, partnering closely with accounting personnel to ensure alignment with accounting standards.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and refine models, incorporating key drivers to assess and drive performance.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide clear insight into trends, risks, and opportunities to support proactive decision-making.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a trusted finance partner to senior commercial leadership, advising on bookings, cost of sale, and strategic investment decisions.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally with to assess pipeline health, pricing strategy, and revenue implications.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure robust controls and governance across revenue processes and reporting.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support audit activities and maintain integrity of financial data.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive best practices in NetSuite ERP across all areas of the business; serve as a financial systems resource for Served with Honor.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support audit activities and maintain integrity of financial data.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhance forecasting capabilities through the use of data and AI-driven tools.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-impact role for someone looking to combine strong technical FP&amp;A expertise with real commercial influence in a fast-evolving, global environment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervise, train, and mentor accounting staff.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Works across all levels of the organization to resolve issues, improve processes, and assist in the education and training of staff.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Performs other duties as assigned.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Accounting and/or Finance required.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of progressive accounting and finance experience.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong GAAP and variance analysis expertise.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with NetSuite ERP systems preferred.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to lead and manage Finance staff and cross-functional teams.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical, financial modeling, and communication skills; advanced Excel required; Power BI or similar reporting tools a plus.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to work effectively with all levels of the organization.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing and optimizing Accounting and Finance technology platforms.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication, coaching, and relationship-building skills</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think strategically while executing effectively in a fast-paced, evolving environment.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to build, develop, and lead high-performing teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Physical Demands:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to stand, sit, use of hands to handle, feel, or reach with hands and arms.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to lift and/ or move up to 15 pounds.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and distance vision.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Environment:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote office environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"Positions Summary:\n\nWe are seeking an experienced Finance Manager to join our team in a fast-paced services environment. This is a key role responsible for ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial plans and forecasts, systems, and reporting while supporting strategic decision-making across the organization. \n \nAs a trusted business partner to the Chief Financial Officer and Senior Leadership Team, the Finance Manager will lead all aspects of financial planning and analysis while contributing to accounting and operational analysis. This role oversees the budgeting and forecasts process including variance analysis while also operating as key resources in the monthly and annual close process.  \n \nThe ideal candidate will bring strong financial leadership, the ability to translate financial data into actionable insights and a deep understanding of NetSuite and financial systems. This position plays a critical role in strengthening financial controls, driving continuous improvement, and optimizing profitability while supporting effective cost management throughout the business. \n\n\n\nSupervisory Responsibilities:\n\nSupervises employees in the Accounting and Finance department. Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization's policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring, training employees, planning, assigning, and directing work.\n\n\n\nEssential Functions and Responsibilities: Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\n - Own and lead the revenue, expense and cash forecasting process, partnering closely with accounting personnel to ensure alignment with accounting standards.\n\n - Develop and refine models, incorporating key drivers to assess and drive performance.\n\n - Provide clear insight into trends, risks, and opportunities to support proactive decision-making.\n\n - Act as a trusted finance partner to senior commercial leadership, advising on bookings, cost of sale, and strategic investment decisions.\n\n - Work cross-functionally with to assess pipeline health, pricing strategy, and revenue implications.\n\n - Ensure robust controls and governance across revenue processes and reporting.\n\n - Support audit activities and maintain integrity of financial data.\n\n - Drive best practices in NetSuite ERP across all areas of the business; serve as a financial systems resource for Served with Honor.\n\n - Support audit activities and maintain integrity of financial data.\n\n - Enhance forecasting capabilities through the use of data and AI-driven tools.\n\n - This is a high-impact role for someone looking to combine strong technical FP&A expertise with real commercial influence in a fast-evolving, global environment.\n\n - Supervise, train, and mentor accounting staff.\n\n - Works across all levels of the organization to resolve issues, improve processes, and assist in the education and training of staff.\n\n - Performs other duties as assigned.\n\n\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Accounting and/or Finance required.\n\n - 5+ years of progressive accounting and finance experience.\n\n - Strong GAAP and variance analysis expertise.\n\n - Experience with NetSuite ERP systems preferred.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to lead and manage Finance staff and cross-functional teams.\n\n - Strong analytical, financial modeling, and communication skills; advanced Excel required; Power BI or similar reporting tools a plus.\n\n - Proven ability to work effectively with all levels of the organization.\n\n - Experience implementing and optimizing Accounting and Finance technology platforms.\n\n - Exceptional communication, coaching, and relationship-building skills\n\n - Ability to think strategically while executing effectively in a fast-paced, evolving environment.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build, develop, and lead high-performing teams.\n\n\n\nPhysical Demands:\n\n - Ability to stand, sit, use of hands to handle, feel, or reach with hands and arms.\n\n - Ability to lift and/ or move up to 15 pounds.\n\n - Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and distance vision.\n\n\n\nWork Environment:\n\n - Remote office environment\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9563cb26-ffad-42b8-8eee-60e3e317ad90","title":"Business Intelligence Manager ","department":"Technology","team":"Technology","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote (US)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-09T14:53:59.875+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Austin"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/9563cb26-ffad-42b8-8eee-60e3e317ad90","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ServedWithHonor/9563cb26-ffad-42b8-8eee-60e3e317ad90/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Positions Summary: </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Business Intelligence Manager will be responsible for overseeing and enhancing the operations efficiency and effectiveness of our company. Your expertise in business intelligence and data-driven decision-making will be crucial in identifying opportunities for improvement, streamlining processes, and driving informed strategic choices. You will work closely with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless collaboration, efficient resource allocation, and achievement of key performance indicators. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Essential Functions and Responsibilities: </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Utilizes your experience in business intelligence tools and techniques to gather, analyze and interpret complex data sets</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Provides actionable insights and recommendations to executive management for improved decision-making, resource allocation and process optimization</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Identifies operational bottlenecks, inefficiencies, and areas for improvement within various departments</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Develops and implements strategies to streamline processes, reduce costs and enhance overall operational performance</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Collaborates with department heads and executive management to establish key performance indicators (KPIs) that align with the company’s strategic goals</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Monitors and analyzes KPIs to identify trends, deviations and opportunities and provides regular reports to guide decision-making</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Fosters effective communication and collaboration across departments to ensure smooth workflows and coordinated efforts</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Works closely with teams such as Finance, Marketing, Sales, and Operations to align operations with overall business objectives</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Leads and oversees the implementation of process improvement initiatives and operational projects</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Defines project scope, objectives, timelines, and resource requirements to ensure successful execution within established parameters </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">.• Monitors resource allocation across departments to optimize staffing levels and allocation of assets</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Makes recommendations for resource adjustments based on data driven insights</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Identifies potential operational risks and develops mitigation strategies</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Ensures compliance with industry regulations and company policies minimizing potential disruptions to operations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Stays updated on industry best practices, emerging technologies, and advancements in business intelligence</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Applies knowledge to continuously enhancing operational processes and maintains a competitive edge</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> • Other projects and duties as assigned </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Exceptional ability to deliver concise, incisive, logical written documents and has the presence to deliver recommendations effectively to demanding audiences</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to identify the organization’s strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Comfortable working in a diverse environment with the ability to deal with ambiguity while adapting easily to rapidly changing business conditions</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to adapt and adjust to changing situations</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● A high degree of self-confidence and perseverance and can earn the confidence of others</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to work quickly and efficiently, while under pressure</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Excellent communication, presentation and project management skills</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to multitask and work toward several milestones on various projects simultaneously</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Experience with knowledge of all state and local law</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Competency with Microsoft Office Suite Required </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Bachelor’s degree in related field</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● 5+ years’ experience in data analysis, business intelligence or a related field</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Expertise in SQL, Excel and other data analysis tools</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● String understanding of statistical methods and modeling</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to develop creative solutions to complex problems</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Service-oriented, and a collaborative influence style</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Proven ability to craft and present a business analysis’</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Experience making decisions based on business metrics </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Physical Demands:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to stand, sit, use of hands to handle, feel, or reach with hands and arms</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Ability to lift and/ or move up to 25 pounds</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and distance vision </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Environment:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> ● The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Served with Honor is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, disability or any other basis prohibited by law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Positions Summary: \n\nThe Business Intelligence Manager will be responsible for overseeing and enhancing the operations efficiency and effectiveness of our company. Your expertise in business intelligence and data-driven decision-making will be crucial in identifying opportunities for improvement, streamlining processes, and driving informed strategic choices. You will work closely with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless collaboration, efficient resource allocation, and achievement of key performance indicators. \n\n\n\nEssential Functions and Responsibilities: \n\nReasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\n • Utilizes your experience in business intelligence tools and techniques to gather, analyze and interpret complex data sets\n\n • Provides actionable insights and recommendations to executive management for improved decision-making, resource allocation and process optimization\n\n • Identifies operational bottlenecks, inefficiencies, and areas for improvement within various departments\n\n • Develops and implements strategies to streamline processes, reduce costs and enhance overall operational performance\n\n • Collaborates with department heads and executive management to establish key performance indicators (KPIs) that align with the company’s strategic goals\n\n • Monitors and analyzes KPIs to identify trends, deviations and opportunities and provides regular reports to guide decision-making\n\n • Fosters effective communication and collaboration across departments to ensure smooth workflows and coordinated efforts\n\n • Works closely with teams such as Finance, Marketing, Sales, and Operations to align operations with overall business objectives\n\n • Leads and oversees the implementation of process improvement initiatives and operational projects\n\n • Defines project scope, objectives, timelines, and resource requirements to ensure successful execution within established parameters \n\n.• Monitors resource allocation across departments to optimize staffing levels and allocation of assets\n\n • Makes recommendations for resource adjustments based on data driven insights\n\n • Identifies potential operational risks and develops mitigation strategies\n\n • Ensures compliance with industry regulations and company policies minimizing potential disruptions to operations\n\n • Stays updated on industry best practices, emerging technologies, and advancements in business intelligence\n\n • Applies knowledge to continuously enhancing operational processes and maintains a competitive edge\n\n • Other projects and duties as assigned \n\n\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n\n ● Exceptional ability to deliver concise, incisive, logical written documents and has the presence to deliver recommendations effectively to demanding audiences\n\n ● Ability to identify the organization’s strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats\n\n ● Comfortable working in a diverse environment with the ability to deal with ambiguity while adapting easily to rapidly changing business conditions\n\n ● Ability to adapt and adjust to changing situations\n\n ● A high degree of self-confidence and perseverance and can earn the confidence of others\n\n ● Ability to work quickly and efficiently, while under pressure\n\n ● Excellent communication, presentation and project management skills\n\n ● Ability to multitask and work toward several milestones on various projects simultaneously\n\n ● Experience with knowledge of all state and local law\n\n ● Competency with Microsoft Office Suite Required \n\n\n\nQualifications:\n\n ● Bachelor’s degree in related field\n\n ● 5+ years’ experience in data analysis, business intelligence or a related field\n\n ● Expertise in SQL, Excel and other data analysis tools\n\n ● String understanding of statistical methods and modeling\n\n ● Ability to develop creative solutions to complex problems\n\n ● Service-oriented, and a collaborative influence style\n\n ● Proven ability to craft and present a business analysis’\n\n ● Experience making decisions based on business metrics \n\n\n\nPhysical Demands:\n\n ● Ability to stand, sit, use of hands to handle, feel, or reach with hands and arms\n\n ● Ability to lift and/ or move up to 25 pounds\n\n ● Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and distance vision \n\n\n\nWork Environment:\n\n ● The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate\n\n\n\nServed with Honor is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, disability or any other basis prohibited by law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$110K – $125K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$110K - $125K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0f534186-81d2-4572-bd73-b4046180225c","tierSummary":"Base Salary $110K – $125K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6816c33e-16ed-4ae3-8d8a-4bee24394261","summary":"Base Salary $110K – $125K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":125000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":125000}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}